                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Dr. Watson wants his money back. Holmes cracked it in minutes, but the murderess still wanted a second opinion.[/h1]\r\n\r\nThe Sherlock Holmes Consulting Detective series are actually not very good games. They show their age quite well and are crying out for remasters that will most likely never happen.\r\n\r\nThe FMV sequences are fun to watch but the acting wasn't really all that good. The main gameplay is basically just guessing who to talk to next. Discovering clues felt like such a chore or maybe it was just way over my head. Some of the achievements are very hard to figure out or at least feel impossible at times because they can be boring but at least a guide makes them easy to get.\r\n\r\nOverall I didn't enjoy this series much at all and don't recommend it unless you're a die hard Sherlock Holmes fan or a glutton for punishment looking to get all the achievements.\r\n\r\n[h2]5/10[/h2]\r\n\r\n[h2][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45905648-Gork%2527s-Game-Grind/]Check out my curated list of games[/url][/h2]",
